 as the Hulk the report states  that a month ago when they broke the  report about some she-hulk  details they had heard rumors about Mark  Ruffalo signing up to be on the series  but they didn't get an official  confirmation so they didn't leak the  scoop however they now say that Mark  Ruffalo is signed sealed and delivered  for the she-hulk series coming to Disney  Plus the report says apparently Mark  Ruffalo has been playing coy and he's  already formally set and signed to  return to his iconic role  the she-hulk Show for Disney Plus  clearly our next question was what the  contract details were in regards to the  number of episodes and if this  negotiation was solely for the small  screen however we weren't able to get  that defined quite yet so Mark Ruffalo  is coming back as the Hulk for the  she-hulk series but is most likely  coming back for way more than that Red  Hulk is already confirmed to be coming  to the MCU relatively soon and it would  make perfect sense for Red Hulk to fight  the Hulk especially if you consider the  connection from The Incredible Hulk  which is canon to the MCU but let's talk  about the biggest thing that could be  coming to the MCU and that would be a  movie with the Hulk and Wolverine now  we've actually had quite a few different  reports on this and Mark Ruffalo himself  has even commented on it several times  as well now all the way back in November  at Tokyo Comic Con Mark Ruffalo made an  appearance and he talked about the  future of the Hulk in the MCU and what  he would like to see he also named  dropped Hulk vs. Wolverine and said that  he would like to see that happen in the  MCU and that he had a meeting with Kevin  Feige lined up where he was going to  pitch him ideas so in November at Tokyo  Comic Con he said Kevin Feige just asked  me last week if I had any more ideas or  stories for the Hulk and I said yeah I  think there's still some stories to tell  and he said well why don't you come in  and tell me about them and we'll see if  we can find a place for you in the  Marvel Universe and then Mark Ruffalo  said I'd like to see that Hulk vs.  Wolverine but then just a week ago Mark  Ruffalo brought this up again when he  was talking about the future of the Hulk  now at this point in time remember that  the Illuminati has said that he was  already signed up to play the Hulk in  the she-hulk series and at c2e2 he'd let  us know what he would like to see from  the Hulk at c2e2 a week ago he first  said that Universal does still have the  rights to the Hulk so they can't do a  solo hulk film however they can do a  solo hulk project if it's streaming or  on disney plus now clearly it's been  announced now that he's going to be on  the she-hulk series however he does go  on to say if he had his way for a Hulk  project this is how he would do it I'd  probably start him off kind of with him  on the run a little bit I think that  really works and in this new digital age  we're all  veiled that may be a kind of interesting  dimension of how he stays on the run  that's probably where we'd start him  saying I don't want to do this anymore  but it's hard now because he's the  professor he's hard to hide he went on  to say to be honest with you I want to  see a movie where Banner and the Hulk  battle it out and then the professor is  sort of a brainchild of that he said  Kevin Feige are you listening we want  professor Hulk the only person that the  Hulk is afraid of is banner and I want  to see the ultimate showdown between the  two of them and maybe Wolverine this  seems to be the ultimate goal for Mark  Ruffalo and the Hulk him taking on  Wolverine in the Marvel Cinematic  Universe and for the first time in an  insanely long time this is an actual  possibility now that Disney owns the  rights to all of the x-men and we know  that Disney is thinking about a way to  introduce these major characters  Wolverine obviously being one of the  biggest ones and it could just be that  introducing Wolverine in a movie with  the Hulk could be the way to do it  Mark Ruffalo wants to do it and  according to a report from Mikey Sutton  months ago the studio's thinking about  doing it as well but Mark Ruffalo is  officially back in the MCU and hopefully  the path that his character goes down in  the MCU leads to Wolverine versus the  Hulk let me know how excited you are  that Mark Ruffalo is officially back in  the MCU as the Hulk and how excited  would you be if we got a Wolverine  versus the Hulk film in the MCU let me  know in the comments down below don't  forget to like the video and subscribe  when notifications turned on to stay up  to date on everything relating to the  MCU as always thank you all so much for  watching  woof woof

